  "response": "# Hotspot triage plan for 04-monorepo\n\nI based this only on the scan output you gave me and didn't open the source files. Churn and recency are 0 on every finding, so there's no git history to go on. The ranking below rests only on structure: who imports what, line counts, and test gap.\n\n## The hotspots at a glance\n\n| File | Fan-in | Fan-out | Transitive importers | Size findings | Test gap |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `src/utils.ts` | **18** (p99 = 10) | 1 | 29 | 424-line file | 0 |\n| `src/index.ts` | 4 | **17** (p99 = 11) | 7 | 459-line file; `build` 293, `<anonymous>` 274, `mainTasks` 194, `normalizeOptions` 96, `startWatcher` 79, `buildAll` 75 | 0 |\n| `src/esbuild/index.ts` | 1 | **11** (= p99) | 7 | `runEsbuild` 237 lines, 38 option properties | 0 |\n| `src/plugin.ts` | 10 (9 type-only) | 3 | 29 | `buildFinished` 103 lines | 0.75 |\n| `src/log.ts` | 9 (4 type-only) | 0 | 30 | — | 0.75 |\n| `src/rollup.ts` | 0 | 7 | 0 | `getRollupConfig` 122 lines | 0.75 |\n| `src/api-extractor.ts` | 1 | 6 (= p95 cutoff) | 7 | `rollupDtsFiles` 85 lines | 0.75 |\n| `test/utils.ts` | 9 | 0 | 9 | — | 0 |\n\n## Refactor first, in order\n\n**1. `src/utils.ts`: the biggest blast radius in the repo.**\n- Fan-in is 18, nearly twice the p99 cutoff of 10, and 29 files import it directly or indirectly. It's also a 424-line file (crime_00068).\n- Any edit here can reach most of `src/`. Splitting it by responsibility means each importer depends on a smaller surface, which directly shrinks future blast radius.\n- Test gap is 0, so you have a safety net.\n- **Do first, before the split:** fix `jsoncParse`, which catches errors with an empty catch and returns `{}` (crime_00043). A broken tsconfig or package.json then looks like \"no config\" to all 29 transitive importers. It's a small fix with the widest reach of any finding.\n- **How to split:** create the new modules and have `utils.ts` re-export them for now. Move the 18 importers over in small batches rather than one big rewrite.\n\n**2. `src/index.ts`: the most concentrated complexity.**\n- Fan-out is 17, the highest in the repo. Six oversized functions are nested inside each other, with `build` at 293 lines, 4.9× the threshold.\n- Fan-in is only 4, so the refactor stays mostly inside this file while greatly reducing what an editor has to keep in their head.\n- Test gap is 0.\n- **Approach:** pull `normalizeOptions`, `buildAll`, `startWatcher` and `mainTasks` out into their own modules so `build` just coordinates them. That also spreads the 17 outgoing imports across smaller files.\n- While you're there, rename or split `build` and `buildAll`. Both have side effects (`removeFiles`) behind names that sound like pure transformations (crime_00014, crime_00015).\n\n**3. `src/esbuild/index.ts`: contained and well tested.**\n- Fan-out is 11 (right at p99) but fan-in is 1, so callers barely notice changes. Test gap is 0.\n- `runEsbuild` is 237 lines and reads 38 properties off one options object (crime_00017).\n- Typing that options object into named sub-records is the highest-value change. It also makes step 2 easier, since `index.ts` is what feeds it options.\n\n**4. `src/plugin.ts`: only the `buildFinished` method body.**\n- `buildFinished` is 103 lines with 29 transitive importers. But test gap is 0.75, so **write tests before refactoring**.\n- Don't touch the module's exports. 9 of its 10 importers take types only, which makes it a shared type hub, and being depended on is its job.\n\n## Leave alone, or defer\n\n- **`src/log.ts`: leave alone.** Fan-in is 9 with fan-out 0, and the scan found nothing else in it. It's a pure leaf utility, and its 30 transitive importers are a reason *not* to touch it. Treat it as load-bearing.\n- **`src/plugin.ts` module structure: leave alone.** Its high fan-in is compile-time type coupling, not a defect.\n- **`test/utils.ts`: leave alone structurally.** It's a shared test helper (fan-in 9, test files only), so production code isn't affected. At most, cap the unbounded `Promise.all` that creates directories and writes files (crime_00020).\n- **`src/rollup.ts`: defer.** `getRollupConfig` is a real 122-line God Function and has a misleading name (crime_00003). But fan-in is 0 and blast radius is 0, so refactoring it does nothing to reduce blast radius. Its test gap is also 0.75. Do it later as cleanup.\n- **`src/api-extractor.ts`: defer.** Fan-out of 6 only just meets the p95 cutoff and fan-in is 1, so it's a weak hotspot. If you're in the file anyway, fix `rollupDtsFiles` (85 lines) and the swallowed error (crime_00018).\n- **`src/cli-main.ts` `main`: defer.** It's 153 lines (crime_00044), but fan-in is only 2 and test gap is 0.75. Tests come before any extraction.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- **The scan's own ranking points the other way.** Its `agent_risk` score puts the size and connectivity findings near the bottom (0.06–0.16) and things like return-shape issues near the top. This plan ranks by blast radius instead, as you asked, so it deliberately differs from that order.\n- **\"effort: small\" understates the big functions.** The scan rates every `large_function` finding as small effort. That isn't realistic for `build` (293 lines) or `runEsbuild` (237 lines), so plan each of those as a multi-step job.",
